  <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="mainLayout">
   <item>
    <widget class="QGroupBox" name="gbAssistantModes">
     <property name="title">
      <string>Relative Position Input Modes</string>
     </property>
     <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="layModes">
      <item>
       <widget class="QLabel" name="label">
        <property name="text">
         <string>The Relative Point Input Assistant is an interactive, on-screen helper overlay that simplifies the process of placing new coordinates relative to the last active point (Relative Zero) without needing to type syntax blindly into the command line.&lt;br&gt;Relative Point Input Assistant is available in any place where coordinate is requested by the active command and could be invoked by keyboard shortcuts (configured by Keyboard Shortcuts settings).</string>
        </property>
        <property name="wordWrap">
         <bool>true</bool>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item>
       <widget class="QCheckBox" name="cbRelativePositionAssistantRememberMode">
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Use Last Used Mode

If checked, used coordinates entering mode will be saved
and retained across consecutive point input prompts.
Otherwise, explicitly specified mode will be used on next invocation.</string>
        </property>
        <property name="text">
         <string>Remember last used coordinates mode</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item>
       <widget class="QCheckBox" name="cbRelativePositionAssistantStartInOffsetMode">
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Relative (Offset) or Absolute Mode

If selected, on invocation the assistant will be in relative coordinates (offset) mode. 
Otherwise, it will prompt to enter absolute coordinates.</string>
        </property>
        <property name="text">
         <string>Start in offset mode</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
     </layout>
    </widget>
   </item>
